@startuml
!pragma useVerticalIf on
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 17
skinparam ArrowColor #46566F
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #EEFAF4
  BorderColor #2E7156
  FontColor #143C2D
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3D6
  DiamondBorderColor #A77D24
  StartColor #2E7156
  EndColor #2E7156
}
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8E8
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C9A34C
title sympy | Symbolic computation workflow
start
:Define the mathematical goal;
:Create symbols with needed assumptions\n(real, positive, integer, ...);
:Construct expressions using exact values;
note right
  Use Rational(...) or S(...) for exact arithmetic.
  Floating-point literals create approximations.
  GUIDE.md: Working with SymPy
end note
if (Solving equations?) then (yes)
  :Select a solver for the equation type;
  note right
    Algebraic: solveset / solve
    Linear systems: linsolve
    Nonlinear systems: nonlinsolve
    Differential equations: dsolve
    references/core-capabilities.md
  end note
  :Substitute solutions and simplify\nto verify the original equations;
else (other computation)
  :Choose the relevant operation;
  note right
    Algebra / calculus: core-capabilities.md
    Matrices: matrices-linear-algebra.md
    Physics: physics-mechanics.md
    Geometry / number theory / logic / statistics:
      advanced-topics.md
  end note
endif
:Compute and simplify symbolically;
if (Result or simplification is unexpected?) then (yes)
  :Review symbol assumptions, float inputs\nand the chosen solver / simplification;
  note right
    GUIDE.md: Troubleshooting Common Issues
    If no closed form exists, consider a
    numerical solver when the goal allows it.
  end note
else (no)
endif
if (Need numerical evaluation?) then (yes)
  if (Many repeated evaluations?) then (yes)
    :Use lambdify(..., 'numpy')\nfor array-based evaluation;
  else (single / precision)
    :Use evalf(...) / N(...)\nwith the requested precision;
  endif
else (keep exact)
  :Retain symbolic expressions / rationals;
endif
:Return expressions, print LaTeX,\nor generate executable code as needed;
note right
  references/code-generation-printing.md
  Full API examples and caveats: GUIDE.md
end note
stop
@enduml
